# The Drayman's Horse — swamp T2 basic striker (revenant horse, skull-headed)

+title The Drayman's Horse
+image monsters/swamp_beast_1.png
+blood #3a3024
+stats hp=18

+move Attack
  narration: It snaps the human jaw shut on whatever it can reach.
  narration: The neck cants too far for a horse's neck and the skull comes around for you.

+move Defend
  narration: It plants its forelegs and the harness cinches tighter around its flanks.

+move Recover
  narration: The bones reset themselves a little, the way old harness re-knots itself in the dark.

+move Brutal Heavy Slow Telegraphed Attack
  narration: It does not slow. The harness flaps wet against its flanks, and it runs through where you are, and it does not yield the road.

+intro
You hear the wheels first. There are no wheels. The thing comes up the
old hauling track at a pace too steady to be alive — horse-bodied, the
harness rotted on its flanks, the head a human skull set wrong on the
long neck. There is nothing pulling it. There is nothing it is pulling.
It does not slow when it sees you. It has been on this run since before
the village was built, and it does not yield the road.

+win
> gold 10
> tag killed_draymans_horse
Whatever was driving it through its run-without-end has finished
running. The bones come apart on the planks one piece at a time, the
way old harness comes apart, and the human skull goes last and without
ceremony. The hauling track is quiet. It was not, before.

+lose
It does not slow. The hauling track takes you the way the hauling track
takes anything that does not yield it.
